// Title: VeeamBackup Database Credentials Dump Via Sqlcmd.EXE
// Sigma ID: b57ba453-b384-4ab9-9f40-1038086b4e53
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: frack113
// Date: 2021-12-20 | Modified: 2023-02-13
// ATT&CK: collection, T1005
// Description: Detects dump of credentials in VeeamBackup dbo
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://thedfirreport.com/2021/12/13/diavol-ransomware/
//   - https://forums.veeam.com/veeam-backup-replication-f2/recover-esxi-password-in-veeam-t34630.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_sqlcmd_veeam_dump.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\sqlcmd.exe" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "SELECT" and ProcessCommandLine contains "TOP" and ProcessCommandLine contains "[VeeamBackup].[dbo].[Credentials]")
